  "question": {
    "text": "A red solid is insoluble in water. However it becomes soluble if some $\\mathrm{KI}$ is added to water. Heating the red solid in a test tube results in liberation of some violet coloured fumes and droplets of a metal appear on the cooler parts of the test tube. The red solid is",
    "image": null
  },
